    "@value" : "Counseling designed to guide and support an individual to overcome alcohol dependence."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid415",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref" : [ {
    "@value" : "NCIT:C66930"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000653"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "A pharmaceutical agent that selectively inhibits angiotensin II receptor activation in the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. It is primarily used for the reduction of proteinuria and the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid416",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref" : [ {
    "@value" : "NCIT:C66930"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000653"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "Angiotensin II receptor antagonists bind to and block the activation of angiotensin II type 1 (AT1) receptors, thereby reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. Although this class of agents is also used in diabetic nephropathy (kidney damage due to diabetes) and congestive heart failure, it is primarily used for the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid417",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "The National Health Service (NHS). https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/alcohol-misuse/"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/afmo#AlcoholMisuse"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Alcohol misuse is when you drink in a way that's harmful, or when you're dependent on alcohol."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid418",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "Mayo Clinic, https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/atrial-fibrillation/symptoms-causes/syc-20350624, accessed 14 July 2026."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/afmo#AtrialFibrillationEpisode"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "A period of time during which \"the heart's upper chambers, called the atria, beat chaotically and irregularl [...] out of sync with the lower heart chambers, called the ventricles.\""
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid419",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "Oxford Refence https://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/oi/authority.20110803095759525, accessed 09 July 2026."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/afmo#RaceOrEthnicity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "Ethnicity is a term for the ethnic group to which people belong. Usually it refers to group identity based on culture, religion, traditions, and customs. In some contexts, it is a “politically correct” term equivalent to the word “race,” which may have pejorative associations."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid420",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "The National Human Genome Research Institute. https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Race"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/afmo#RaceOrEthnicity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "Race is a social construct used to group people. Race was constructed as a hierarchal human-grouping system, generating racial classifications to identify, distinguish and marginalize some groups across nations, regions and the world. Race divides human populations into groups often based on physical appearance, social factors and cultural backgrounds."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid421",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nhis/tobacco/tobacco_recodes.htm#anchor_1557516509294 and the New Zealand Ministry of Health https://www.health.govt.nz/our-work/preventative-health-wellness/tobacco-control/tobacco-control-information-practitioners/definitions-smoking-status.\n\n- Smoker (a.k.a current smoker): a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes (including hand rolled cigarettes, cigars, cigarillos etc) in their lifetime and has smoked in the last 28 days. Includes daily and non-daily/social smokers.\n- Non-smoker: composed of two groups: former smoker and never smoker.\n   - Former smoker: a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime but has not smoked in the last 28 days. The international convention is to treat someone as an ex-smoker once they have been smokefree for one month (at least 28 days).\n   - Never smoker: a person who has not smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime and does not currently smoke.\n\nDagfinn et al. (2018) noted that there is reduced risk of AF among former smokers compared to current smokers, but further research is needed to determine if the risk at some point reaches that of never smokers."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/afmo#SmokingStatus"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A person's cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "_:genid422",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy" : [ {
    "@value" : "McClure, Robert C., et al. \"Gender harmony: improved standards to support affirmative care of gender-marginalized people through inclusive gender and sex representation.\" Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 29.2 (2022): 354-363. https://doi-org.ezproxy.uct.ac.za/10.1093/jamia/ocab196"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedProperty" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedSource" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.org/phmo#Sex"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#annotatedTarget" : [ {
    "@value" : "Summary sex classification element based on one or more clinical observations such as an organ survey, hormone levels, and chromosomal analysis."
